#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:207
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`changes needed` goes back to the author and the reworked DAK is assembled again; `validated` records the adjudication. Assembly does not wait for this decision."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:234
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "`claimed`: the bean is in progress and this process works it. `not yours`: a sibling session or a person holds it, nothing was written to it, and this process stops (bean-coordination)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:212
#. Diagram label
msgid "Assemble and validate the DAK"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:213
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Assemble the validated components and run content validation: schemas, cross-component consistency and terminology bindings. The smart-base extractors read the authored artefacts; with SMART_BASE_HOME unset they report skip, never a clean run."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:138
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the DAK's L2 business processes as BPMN 2.0 with Diagram Interchange: a .bpmn with no x/y on its shapes renders blank. Stay at L2, reviewable by a clinician, not FHIR. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the BPMN inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: bpmn-js import with no warnings, dak-swimlanes.ts, artefact-reachability; renderer: render:bpmn with a visual-diff before/after; reviewer: clinical SME)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:129
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the DAK's personas and the user scenarios they appear in. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the personas-and-scenarios inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: dak-swimlanes.ts and traceability to L1 recommendations; renderer: the persona card and a prose diff; reviewer: clinical SME). These are the DAK's own actors, not this harness's scenarios/roles.json; do not conflate the two."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:156
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the data dictionary and core data elements: structured but not FHIR, reviewable by a clinician, so L3 can be derived from them rather than written twice. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the glossary inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: check-web-annexes.ts on the data dictionary web annex; renderer: the term diff from dak-data-dictionary-diff.ts and each form's chosen wireframe; reviewer: clinical SME, terminologist for codes)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:147
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the decision and scheduling logic as DMN tables within the FEEL subset the interpreter implements (any, literals, comparisons, one-of); ranges, not() and function calls are refused at load. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the DMN inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: load, reachability, test cases; renderer: dmn2html table before/after, each rule beside its L1 citation; reviewer: clinical SME)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:165
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Author the indicators and the functional and non-functional requirements. These are the DAK's requirements, not skills/requirements/*.json (this harness's own conformance obligations). Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the indicators-and-requirements inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: each names the persona and process it serves and traces to L1; renderer: prose diff; reviewer: business analyst with the programme manager)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:233
#. Diagram label
msgid "Bean claimed?"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:89
#. Diagram label
msgid "Build the L1 library from Component 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:47
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Builds the DAK's L1 library from Component 1 before the work plan is seeded, so every track starts with its guidance in the library and the L1 graph. Opens the parallel fork into six authoring tracks (five in this lane, terminology in its own) and re-enters it whenever clinical validation sends work back, so a fix revisits every entangled track, not only the one the SME flagged. Assembles and validates the DAK in parallel with clinical validation, and again after any rework."
msgstr ""

