msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:39
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Claims the DAK's bean (Process_BeanOpen) once the L1 library is built, then seeds the DAK's work plan with one child bean per component, before the parallel fork. Nothing returns to this lane: the bean is closed at each end (Process_BeanClose), and per-track progress is not tracked here."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:69
#. Diagram label
msgid "Clinical SME"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:198
#. Diagram label
msgid "Clinical validation"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:193
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Clinical validation and assembly start together: adjudication is QA, not a gate. The DAK is assembled and handed to L3 while the SME reviews it; a \"changes needed\" sends the work round again, which re-assembles it."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:70
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Clinical validation runs beside assembly, not before it: QA, not a gate. A \"no\" loops back through Gateway_AuthorMerge into the fork, so this lane decides whether personas, BPMN, DMN, data dictionary and indicators are all revisited together."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:206
#. Diagram label
msgid "Clinically accurate?"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:220
#. Diagram label
msgid "Clinically validated"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:243
#. Diagram label
msgid "Close the bean"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:155
#. Diagram label
msgid "Data dictionary and core data elements"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:146
#. Diagram label
msgid "Decision logic · DMN tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:82
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Enumerate the processes, decisions and data elements the guideline implies; identify the actors."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:199
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Ground truth: does the DAK say what the guideline says? The whole-DAK reading across components: whether personas, processes, decisions, data elements and indicators tell one consistent story. Per-component reviews already happened inside each track (Process_L2ComponentEditReview) and are not repeated."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:27
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a WHO SMART Guidelines L2 Digital Adaptation Kit is authored by a business analyst, a terminologist and a clinical SME under a programme manager. Each of the six authoring tracks calls l2-component-edit-review.bpmn (Process_L2ComponentEditReview): the agent edits, checks, renders and stages the component and hands it on, while a person in the component's reviewing role reviews it alongside, never as a gate. Each track's renderer, checker and reviewer are tabled in the skill l2-component-edit-review."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:175
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "ICD-11, SNOMED CT and LOINC bindings, governed separately from the artefacts that cite them. Calls Process_L2ComponentEditReview with the terminology inputs of the skill l2-component-edit-review (checker: bindings resolve and unmappedConcepts is reported; renderer: the term diff on the code columns; reviewer: a terminologist other than the one who bound it)."
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:164
#. Diagram label
msgid "Indicators and requirements"
msgstr ""

#: ../smart-base/processes/content/l2-dak-authoring.bpmn:90
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Ingest the DAK into the library; it is L2, so it gets no L1 graph. Read Component 1 §1.2 for its sources (extract-dak-l1-references.ts --context-only), fetch each L1 source (fetch-dspace-item.ts for an IRIS handle, fetch-who-publication.ts for a who.int item page) and ingest it. Record on its intake whether each is L1 (declared > context > inferred; --record-context writes §1.2's context). For each L1 source, run l1-specialise.ts: its publication, sections and elements as specialisations of its library nodes, since the library is upstream of L1. Validate with the smart-base Zod validator. Citation fidelity (does each citation name the source it resolves to) and a cited edition older than the one fetched are left to a person, never passed automatically."
msgstr ""

